[ 2026-10-09 17:53:44,249 ] groq._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/openai/v1/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-ac5c2b20-5f26-45ca-bffb-3419ef85fc78', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': "You are an expert Mechanical Engineering Assistant.\n\nProblem Categories: ['shaft_design', 'mechanics', 'factor_of_safety']\nTarget Operations: ['torque', 'power', 'shaft_diameter', 'torsional_stress', 'shear_stress', 'factor_of_safety']\nExtracted Parameters: {'power': 15000.0, 'speed': 1200.0, 'diameter': 0.04, 'bending_moment': 450.0, 'yield_strength': 250000000.0}\nAssociated Units: {'power': 'W', 'speed': 'RPM', 'diameter': 'm', 'bending_moment': 'N*m', 'yield_strength': 'Pa'}\n\nInstructions:\n1. Review the target operations and extracted parameters along with their specific units.\n2. Convert parameter units if needed before performing calculations.\n3. Invoke the necessary calculation/conversion tools using the exact numerical values and appropriate units.\n4. If multiple operations are required, execute all relevant tools in proper sequence.\n5. Do not invent or fabricate missing parameters.\n"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'A solid circular steel shaft transmits a power of 15 kW at 1,200 RPM. The shaft has a diameter of 40 mm and is subjected to a bending moment of 450 N·m in addition to the transmitted torque.\n\nAssume the shaft material has a yield strength of 250 MPa. Neglect stress concentration effects.\n\nUsing the maximum shear stress theory (Tresca), determine:\n\nThe transmitted torque in N·m.\n\nThe maximum bending stress in MPa.\n\nThe maximum torsional shear stress in MPa.\n\nThe maximum shear stress at the outer surface under combined bending and torsion.\n\nThe factor of safety against yielding according to Tresca.\n\nShow the equations, substitutions, units, and final results. Do not assume the shaft is under pure'}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_force', 'description': "Calculate force using Newton's second law.\n\nFormula:\n    F = m * a\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Force in Newtons (N).", 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_mass', 'description': 'Calculate mass from force and acceleration.\n\nFormula:\n    m = F / a\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Mass in kilograms (kg).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_acceleration', 'description': 'Calculate acceleration from force and mass.\n\nFormula:\n    a = F / m\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n\nReturns:\n    Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'mass': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'mass'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_torque', 'description': 'Calculate torque.\n\nFormula:\n    τ = r * F * sin(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    lever_arm: Distance from pivot in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and lever arm in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Torque in Newton-meters (N·m).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'lever_arm': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 90.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'lever_arm'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_work', 'description': 'Calculate mechanical work.\n\nFormula:\n    W = F * d * cos(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    displacement: Displacement in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and displacement in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Work in Joules (J).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'displacement': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 0.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'displacement'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_energy', 'description': 'Calculate kinetic energy.\n\nFormula:\n    KE = 1/2 * m * v²\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    velocity: Velocity in meters per second (m/s).\n\nReturns:\n    Kinetic energy in Joules (J).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'velocity': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'velocity'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_power', 'description': 'Calculate mechanical power.\n\nFormula:\n    P = W / t\n\nArgs:\n    work: Work in Joules (J).\n    time: Time in seconds (s).\n\nReturns:\n    Power in Watts (W).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'work': {'type': 'number'}, 'time': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['work', 'time'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_stress', 'description': 'Calculate normal stress.\n\nFormula:\n    σ = F / A\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    area: Cross-sectional area in square meters (m²).\n\nReturns:\n    Stress in Pascals (Pa).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'area': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'area'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_strain', 'description': 'Calculate normal strain.\n\nFormula:\n    ε = ΔL / L₀\n\nArgs:\n    change_in_length: Change in length in meters (m).\n    original_length: Original length in meters (m).\n\nReturns:\n    Strain (dimensionless).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'change_in_length': {'type': 'number'}, 'original_length': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['change_in_length', 'original_length'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'factor_of_safety', 'description': 'Calculate the factor of safety for an engineering component.\n\nThe factor of safety is calculated as:\n\n    FoS = Material Strength / Applied Stress\n\nOperations:\n    yield_strength:\n        Calculate factor of safety using yield strength.\n\n    ultimate_strength:\n        Calculate factor of safety using ultimate strength.\n\n    applied_stress:\n        Calculate factor of safety using the provided\n        material strength and applied stress.\n\nParameters:\n    operation:\n        Type of factor-of-safety calculation.\n\n    strength:\n        Material strength, such as yield strength or\n        ultimate strength.\n\n    applied_stress:\n        Stress applied to the engineering component.\n\nImportant:\n    strength and applied_stress must use the same units.\n\nExamples:\n    Yield-based FoS:\n        factor_of_safety(\n            operation="yield_strength",\n            strength=250,\n            applied_stress=100\n        )\n\n    Ultimate-based FoS:\n        factor_of_safety(\n            operation="ultimate_strength",\n            strength=400,\n            applied_stress=200\n        )', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['yield_strength', 'ultimate_strength', 'applied_stress'], 'type': 'string'}, 'strength': {'type': 'number'}, 'applied_stress': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['operation', 'strength', 'applied_stress'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'beam_stress', 'description': "Calculate beam stresses and internal forces.\n\nSupported operations:\n\n1. bending_stress\n    Formula:\n        sigma = M * c / I\n\n    Required:\n        moment\n        c\n        inertia\n\n2. shear_stress\n    Formula:\n        tau = V * Q / (I * b)\n\n    Required:\n        force\n        first_moment_area\n        inertia\n        width\n\n3. bending_moment\n    Formula:\n        M = F * d\n\n    Required:\n        force\n        distance\n\n4. shear_force\n    Formula:\n        V = F\n\n    Required:\n        force\n\nParameters:\n    force:\n        Applied or internal force.\n\n    distance:\n        Perpendicular distance from force to the beam's\n        reference point.\n\n    moment:\n        Bending moment.\n\n    c:\n        Distance from the neutral axis to the outermost\n        fiber.\n\n    inertia:\n        Second moment of area (I).\n\n    area:\n        Cross-sectional area.\n\n    first_moment_area:\n        First moment of area (Q).\n\n    width:\n        Cross-sectional width at the location where\n        shear stress is being calculated.\n\nReturns:\n    Calculated engineering quantity as a float.", 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['bending_stress', 'shear_stress', 'bending_moment', 'shear_force'], 'type': 'string'}, 'force': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'distance': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'moment': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'c': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'inertia': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'area': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'first_moment_area': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'width': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}}, 'required': ['operation'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'shaft_design', 'description': 'Design and analyze a solid circular shaft under torque and bending loads.\n\nSupported operations:\n\n1. shaft_diameter\n   Calculate required shaft diameter considering combined bending\n   and torsional loading.\n\n   Bending stress:\n       sigma = 32*M / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Torsional shear stress:\n       tau = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Von Mises equivalent stress:\n       sigma_vm = sqrt(sigma^2 + 3*tau^2)\n\n   Required diameter:\n       d = [\n           (16 / (pi * allowable_stress))\n           * sqrt(4*M^2 + 3*T^2)\n       ]^(1/3)\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       bending_moment\n       allowable_stress\n\n2. torsional_stress\n   Calculate torsional shear stress in a solid circular shaft.\n\n       tau = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       diameter\n\n3. shear_stress\n   Calculate combined transverse and torsional shear stress.\n\n   Torsional shear:\n       tau_t = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Average transverse shear:\n       tau_v = F / A\n\n   Conservative combined shear:\n       tau_total = tau_t + tau_v\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       diameter\n       transverse_force\n       area\n\n4. factor_of_safety\n   Calculate factor of safety using Von Mises stress.\n\n       sigma_b = 32*M / (pi*d^3)\n\n       tau_t = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n       sigma_vm = sqrt(sigma_b^2 + 3*tau_t^2)\n\n       FoS = yield_strength / sigma_vm\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       bending_moment\n       diameter\n       yield_strength\n\nImportant:\n    All quantities must use a consistent unit system.\n\n    Example:\n        torque     -> N*m\n        bending    -> N*m\n        diameter   -> m\n        stress     -> Pa\n        yield      -> Pa\n\n    This implementation assumes a solid circular shaft.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['shaft_diameter', 'torsional_stress', 'shear_stress', 'factor_of_safety'], 'type': 'string'}, 'torque': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'bending_moment': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'diameter': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'allowable_stress': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'yield_strength': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'transverse_force': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'area': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}}, 'required': ['operation'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'pump_power', 'description': 'Calculate pump hydraulic power, shaft power, and pump head.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n1. HYDRAULIC POWER\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nHydraulic power:\n\n    P_h = Q * DeltaP\n\nwhere:\n\n    P_h = hydraulic power [W]\n    Q   = volumetric flow rate [m^3/s]\n    DeltaP = pressure increase [Pa]\n\nHydraulic power can also be calculated from head:\n\n    P_h = rho * g * Q * H\n\nwhere:\n\n    rho = fluid density [kg/m^3]\n    g   = gravitational acceleration [m/s^2]\n    H   = pump head [m]\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n2. SHAFT POWER\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nShaft power is the hydraulic power divided by pump efficiency:\n\n    P_shaft = P_h / eta\n\nTherefore:\n\n    P_shaft = Q * DeltaP / eta\n\nor:\n\n    P_shaft = rho * g * Q * H / eta\n\nwhere:\n\n    eta = pump efficiency\n\nEfficiency must be between 0 and 1.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n3. PUMP HEAD\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nPump head from pressure difference:\n\n    H = DeltaP / (rho * g)\n\nwhere:\n\n    H = pump head [m]\n    DeltaP = pressure difference [Pa]\n    rho = fluid density [kg/m^3]\n    g = gravitational acceleration [m/s^2]\n\nUnits:\n\n    flow_rate        -> m^3/s\n    pressure_difference -> Pa\n    density          -> kg/m^3\n    head             -> m\n    efficiency       -> 0 to 1\n    hydraulic power  -> W\n    shaft power      -> W\n\nAssumptions:\n\n    - 